t ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T02:39:56-07:00","id":919011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/238954-firestorm-alley?p=918404#post918404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather go see that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded.<br /> AKQJT","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T02:54:57-07:00","id":919014,"title":"","content":"Work is a nebulous thing for me. Telling my glorified dick jokes aside, it's a LOT like just being unemployed and making many social media &quot;friends&quot;. My task for this week is making a half dozen calls, sending a few emails and making posters for shows.<br /> I should feel like I'm coasting. I'm looking at it like someone erased all of Minecraft, and then everyone went &quot;YOU rebuild. What, you ask? EVERYTHING.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm just fundamentally lazy. Hopefully I'm just amazing at procrastination.Not sure.<br /> I'm putting every bit of useful energy I've got into working, though.<br /> I want to bring underrated, killer comics to as many people as possible. I'm glad beyond words that comedy is as big and involved in culture as it is now. People really deserve to hear the less heard, though, the Not Yet Approved For Headlining, the underdog. That's the Cute Little Roadkill tour philosophy.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm spending most of next month doing open Mic nights just for some warming up at local-ish places.<br /> <br /> <br /> If anyone's interested in a weird art project, feel free to sketch out whatever the phrase Cute Little Roadkill Comedy looks like to you.<br /> If you wouldn't mind getting your art out there, I'll gladly pay for use of the image if it fits the tour well enough. I'd love touring with something made by a forumite.<br /> <br /> If any of you live west of the Mississippi and want a weird comedy show to check out, let me know.<br /> I know plenty of lovely oddballs who would play a really spacious backyard or something, unless there was an available venue or course.<br /> <br /> <br /> (.I sound so far up my own ass right now.... *self hatred ACTIVATE!*)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 06-22-2016, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T21:25:49-07:00","id":931800,"title":"","content":"You. Can't. Kill. My. Dreams. Motherfuckers.<br /> <br /> I'll trade blows with the triat, Sol Invictus and Caine just to make my stupid dream come true. I can't give in. This is my life.... this is my life..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T23:51:05-07:00","id":931858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/238954-firestorm-alley?p=931800#post931800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You. Can't. Kill. My. Dreams. Motherfuckers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn straight they can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T20:32:44-07:00","id":1114383,"title":"","content":"It's Monday here, but it's already Tuesday most places, so I'll play your time zone game and say it's Tuesday morning. It's not a big deal. I keep track of the day like I keep track of most things. Poorly. <br /> <br /> That's how I've been doing since last summer, too. Truth be told, I'm a little bit more broken than I ever used to be, at least the way I see it. I can't say that I didn't make terrible, stupid choices about how I was living at the time, as a heavy drinking, drug abusing master of ruined ceremonies. However I got to the point of true vulnerability, though, that's where I fell. Where I got pushed over a cliff's edge that I barely knew I had.<br /> <br /> In late July of last year (wasn't 2016 a great year? I'm literally still getting over it. You?) I was engaged (yes, again. I don't get me either) to someone that I had been introduced to years ago by family. This engagement happened within a week or two of having drinks together. The time is quite blurry in places, because I was sober for very little of the whole relationship. My family and friends got fed lines about sudden romance, but I was in an environment where I could eat painkillers and wash them down with liquor. I was treated like shit, but I was in Self-Destructive Heaven. And then the line, my line of safety that I've had since I was young, was crossed.<br /> <br /> ...I started drinking and self medicating to numb myself from emotional pain, from trauma and the things about myself that can't be easily changed, if at all. I have my guard up against the whole of humanity by default, though I try to work on that. Drinking let the shields down, let me forget about my worries and anxieties relating to my safety. Before the month was over, I'd moved in with then, become engaged, done enough drugs and drinking to kill a less sturdy human being, and snapped like a twig psychologically after a drunken assault.<br /> <br /> After it occurred, I checked myself into a psychiatric ward, for my safety and that of others. My post traumatic mind was borderline homicidal in its defensiveness. I hadn't been that afraid of what I could be capable of in years, if ever. I had to flee my abuser, and I knew it was because I couldn't trust myself to not hurt them in return. Probably permanently. Into the psych ward I went, then, and I've been doing outpatient therapy and trying to get myself together ever since. <br /> <br /> I've been trying to pursue work and my hobbies more, gaming and writing more, to help me deal with the things I'm going through and also to help me to remember that there are things, and people, that I still love, trust and care about.<br /> <br /> Life has been strange and rather unsettling in the last year. I think many people could agree on that particular. I'm still working on becoming a fully professional comedy something or other, though. I'm still running and playing WoD, especially my old friend, VtM. ... I'm still trying.<br /> <br /> I think that counts for something. I hope so, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:31:32-07:00","id":1115380,"title":"","content":"Stop for a moment.<br /> <br /> Breathe.<br /> <br /> Calm down.<br /> <br /> What's the big deal?<br /> <br /> You hear this from time to time when in emotional situations, and it's a logical response in its way. It's straightforward in that, on a base level, whoever is saying it does want the problematic situation to end, if only to remove an annoyance. People avoid and ignore, on average, a great many things that impact them personally, so the sentiment behind most &quot;just get over it&quot; responses says much about how we internalize this cognitive blind spot that masks itself as some aggressive form of stoicism. <br /> <br /> If I picked a specific issue to attach this to, I think I might miss my own point. As much as I'd like to defend my personal position on things, shouting from a cute little soapbox, this response comes from people on many, hell, most sides depending on the issue. We dismiss each other's experiences, and are likely poorer in spirit for it. I can't even point to a chunk of the globe and say &quot;this is a problem HERE&quot; because here is the world. We're all connected, and each of us human beings has their opinions. When we agree, we're agreeing across borders and oceans. When we don't, we argue across them. That works for me.<br /> <br /> We're not the machines we communicate through, though (possible exceptions being that one AI which was guided into racism, and Short Circuit's Johnny 5, because he's alive) and we're generally emotional creatures. We have moments where our feelings obscure context or blind us to sense. We know that, fundamentally, about ourselves as a species.<br /> <br /> ..and yet we still tell one another, as if on cue, to stop, take a moment, and breathe. Calm down, they say. I know I've repeated that line myself more than a few times. Calm down, as if it was that easy. A simple act of will.<br /> <br /> What's the big deal? I have an issue, and I'm a person, like you. That's what. Our issues matter. Let's stop shutting each other up. It silences everyone in the end, and we still have much to discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T18:16:07-07:00","id":1116188,"title":"","content":"Ripping off Bill Maher here, but<br /> <br /> NEW RULE: We can't be one world until we all agree what fucking time it is! No more time zones. We will all agree on a planetary time and just deal with whatever the fuck the sky is doing, like adults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T09:56:47-07:00","id":1116449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/238954-firestorm-alley?p=1116188#post1116188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ripping off Bill Maher here, but<br /> <br /> NEW RULE: We can't be one world until we all agree what fucking time it is! No more time zones. We will all agree on a planetary time and just deal with whatever the fuck the sky is doing, like adults.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Switch to a 24 hour clock. Make it planet standard time. If its 8 and the suns up on march 1st. Then its 8 and sundown on march 1st no am pm timezone crap<br /> None of that annoying as hell its &quot;its tommorow where i am, so did you mean today?&quot; Yano?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T03:36:01-07:00","id":1142449,"title":"","content":"Sleep is coming slow. I feel like a bored and frustrated teenager waiting for the city bus, my angst still fresh. I feel like chainsmoking while a horror movie plays in the background, my entire being focused on spinning a yarn that'll creep my friends out and be talked about like our own private war after the game was over. It's a feeling that's in need of revitalization. <br /> Now, I have not and likely will not enjoy the majority of the works of Def Leppard, for reasons I myself can't fully explain. That aside, they made a point; that it's better to burn out than to fade away. My life is a chaotic thing, and I sometimes forget that I, much to my intellectual chagrin, am guided by my passions more than by any plan.<br /> I've been operating on the premise that my life has some greater plan, and had forgotten some things that I value because of it. I can't say that I'm going off the rails on a Crazy Train *cue Zakk Wylde ruining one of my favorite guitar solos*, but I'm definitely not on a path. The map has become kindling. I'm wandering, but I refuse to be lost. That's likely due more to ego than resolve, but one takes what one can get. I'm doing things because I want to, and I suppose that's what matters. Eat, drink and be merry, for tomorrow...<br /> <br /> You know the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}